WEBVTT

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.900
Are you a SMART fella,

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.933
or a FART smella?

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.433
Let's find OUT!

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.233
Okay!

00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:11.467
Which one does NOT belong?

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:12.100
A.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:12.767
Apple,

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:13.400
B.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.033
Banana,

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:14.700
C.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.333
Carrot,

00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:16.633
or D.

00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:17.267
Grape?

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.567
Five seconds!

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:25.533
TIME'S UP!

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.500
The answer is...

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:27.933
C,

00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:28.367
carrot!

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:29.233
An apple,

00:00:29.233 --> 00:00:29.667
banana,

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:31.800
and grape are all fruits.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.967
A carrot is a vegetable,

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:36.133
so it does not belong.

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:38.300
Here's one,

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.867
a picture puzzle!

00:00:39.867 --> 00:00:42.467
Which shape completes the pattern?

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:43.000
A.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.567
A filled circle,

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:45.100
B.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.667
An empty triangle,

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:47.167
C.

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:48.733
A filled square,

00:00:48.733 --> 00:00:49.767
or D.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:51.333
A filled triangle?

00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:52.400
Five seconds!

00:00:58.167 --> 00:00:59.367
TIME'S UP!

00:01:00.033 --> 00:01:01.300
The answer is...

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:01.700
D,

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:02.967
a filled triangle!

00:01:02.967 --> 00:01:05.467
The rule is the shape gets

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:07.967
filled in but stays the same

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:08.367
shape,

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.867
so the empty triangle becomes a

00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:11.700
filled triangle.

00:01:12.867 --> 00:01:14.100
Here's one,

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.900
a number series!

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:16.533
One,

00:01:16.533 --> 00:01:17.133
two,

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:17.733
five,

00:01:17.733 --> 00:01:18.333
ten,

00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:18.967
seventeen,

00:01:18.967 --> 00:01:20.167
and then...

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:22.000
what comes next?

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:22.600
A.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:23.233
Twenty-four,

00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:23.833
B.

00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:24.433
Twenty-six,

00:01:24.433 --> 00:01:25.067
C.

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:25.667
Twenty-five,

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:26.867
or D.

00:01:26.867 --> 00:01:27.500
Twenty-eight?

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.700
Five seconds!

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.700
TIME'S UP!

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:38.100
The answer is...

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:38.700
B,

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.267
twenty-six!

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:42.767
The gaps are the odd numbers

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:43.333
one,

00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:43.933
three,

00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:44.500
five,

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:45.067
seven,

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.233
then nine.

00:01:46.233 --> 00:01:49.733
So seventeen plus nine is twenty-six.

00:01:50.867 --> 00:01:51.267
So,

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:53.300
are you smart or fart?

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.733
Count up your correct answers to

00:01:55.733 --> 00:01:56.933
find your rank!

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:58.433
So,

00:01:58.433 --> 00:01:59.833
how did you do?

00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:01.200
Comment your score below,

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.567
and follow for more!
